                <head>No. 197<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On June 16 strikes and demonstrations broke out in East Berlin over increased
                    working norms which had been decreed by the German Democratic Republic. The
                    demonstrations continued in East Berlin and in several other cities in the
                    German Democratic Republic for two days before being suppressed. This series of
                    events led to an exchange of letters between Chancellor Adenauer and President Eisenhower, initiated by the former on June
                    21, concerning rights and conditions in the Soviet Zone.</p>
                <p>For documentation on the demonstrations in Berlin and the texts of the letters
                    exchanged between the Chancellor and the President, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1952-54v07p2/d731">Documents 731</ref> ff.</p>
            </div>
